# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
docker-compose.yml
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
!coverage.go
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Built binary
/mycalendar

# Local SQLite database. It holds real calendar data, so it must never be
# committed; the WAL and shared-memory sidecar files are ignored along with it.
#
# MYCAL_DB accepts any path and SQLite itself accepts several extensions, so
# every plausible spelling is listed: a rule that only covered "*.db" would let
# `MYCAL_DB=./cal.sqlite` commit personal data.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-wal
*.sqlite3-shm
*.db3
*.db3-wal
*.db3-shm

# Frontend dependencies and build output. The bundle is generated: `make build`
# compiles it and embeds it into the binary, so it is never committed.
web/node_modules/
web/e2e/node_modules/
internal/webui/dist/

# Screenshot produced by the optional browser verification.
web/e2e/calendar.png
# A crashed headless browser can drop a core file here.
web/e2e/core

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/
